    "abstract": {
      "en": "Extent of Intact Forest Landscapes (IFLs) in the Caucasus region in 2000. IFLs are large, continuous areas of natural ecosystems without significant human disturbance or fragmentation. The 2000 baseline supports comparison with later IFL assessments to track forest integrity, habitat connectivity, and conservation status across the Caucasus ecoregion.",
